; verify-teardown-dell.run — the Dell (ABIv11) half of the control in
; docs/evidence/midi/verify-teardown.run.
;
; IDENTICAL TO THE RIQEMU1 SCRIPT EXCEPT THE BINARY'S NAME. Same env, same
; song, same clock-out and dev-out, same 1 ms sender task on the same camd
; link. The binary is RIAPP.M4 because that is what this lane stages and
; because a name collision with a previous build is how the wrong binary gets
; run -- the one hazard this lane has already paid for three times.
;
; WHY THIS LANE AT ALL, WHEN THE CRASH WAS ALREADY FIXED AND VERIFIED ON
; riqemu1. Because riqemu1 is ABIv1 and the Dell is ABIv11, and an ABIv11
; binary takes a Software Failure at startup that no ABIv1 build will ever
; show. "It works on the private lane" is not evidence about the Dell; it is
; evidence about a different binary on a different SDK, and this lane is the
; one the owner listens on.
;
; THE PROOF IS NOT THIS SCRIPT EXITING 0. It is: this exits 0 AND the
; --ui-windows check that follows reports no Software Failure, while the same
; sequence against b10e2b7's sources produced one at 327 ms on riqemu1. The
; failure this replaces was `sender_task` calling SendIO every 1 ms on a
; request built by CreateIORequest, which leaves io_Device NULL.

setenv RIAPP_EVLOG RAM:
setenv RIAPP_LOG RAM:
setenv RIAPP_DEMO 0
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_CLKOUT 1
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_DEVOUT 1
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_LATMS 8

Run >NIL: RAM:RIAPP.M4
Wait 20
type RAM:RIAPP-EV.LOG
